ption":{"value":"Map of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armenian_Kingdom_of_Cilicia\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Armenian Kingdom of Cilicia\">Armenian Kingdom of Cilicia</a> during the XIII century."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2008-01-13"},"Artist":{"value":"<div class=\"fn value\">\n<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:S%C3%A9mhur\" title=\"User:Sémhur\">Sémhur</a></div>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}}]},{"pageid":3612392,"title":"File:Cicada molting animated-2.gif","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/62/Cicada_molting_animated-2.gif?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cicada_molting_animated-2.gif","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Animated gif of a cicada (Tibicen sp.) moulting. T. Nathan <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.mundhenk.com\">Mundhenk</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centerville,_Montgomery_County,_Ohio\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Centerville, Montgomery County, Ohio\">Centerville, Ohio</a> USA 30 July 2007. Each frame taken at 1min intervals. 30min gap (middle) as cicada rested. Cicada take appx 2hrs to moult completely."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"30-2007-07"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Mundhenk\" title=\"User:Mundhenk\">T. N. Mundhenk</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY 2.5"}}}]},{"pageid":15763668,"title":"File:Cigaritis cilissa 1.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Cigaritis_cilissa_1.jpg/960px-Cigaritis_cilissa_1.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cigaritis_cilissa_1.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"<i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Cigaritis_cilissa\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Cigaritis cilissa\">Cigaritis cilissa</a></i> foraging on <i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Eryngium_creticum\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Eryngium creticum\">Eryngium creticum</a></i>, Mount Meron, Israel, July 10, 2011."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2011-07-10"},"Artist":{"value":"Gideon Pisanty (<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Gidip\" title=\"User:Gidip\">Gidip</a>) גדעון פיזנטי"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY 3.0"}}}]},{"pageid":23231546,"title":"File:Cicindela marginata Fabricius - ZooKeys-245-001-g012.jpeg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Cicindela_marginata_Fabricius_-_ZooKeys-245-001-g012.jpeg/960px-Cicindela_marginata_Fabricius_-_ZooKeys-245-001-g012.jpeg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cicindela_marginata_Fabricius_-_ZooKeys-245-001-g012.jpeg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Photograph of Cicindela marginata Fabricius. This species is a typical coastal species inhabiting mudflats and salt marshes from New Brunswick to southern Florida and along the Florida Gulf coast; it is also known from the Bahamas and the coast of Cuba. The breeding populations in New Brunswick were discovered only recently. Whether the species had been in the area for some time but went unnoticed, or extended its range in recent years, is the subject of speculation. No size was given for this specimen, but <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" data-mw-original-href=\"http://www.npwrc.usgs.gov/resource/distr/insects/tigb/usa/48.htm\" href=\"https://www.npwrc.usgs.gov/resource/distr/insects/tigb/usa/48.htm\">this source</a> (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.webcitation.org/6Fsg7I3en\">Webcite copy</a>) states \"Common size is 11-14 mm.\""},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2012-12-17 12:47:47"},"Artist":{"value":"Yves Bousquet"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY 3.0"}}}]},{"pageid":25881901,"title":"File:Ciconia ciconia - 01.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Ciconia_ciconia_-_01.jpg/960px-Ciconia_ciconia_-_01.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ciconia_ciconia_-_01.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"White Stork (<i>Ciconia ciconia</i>) in Madrid, Spain."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2013-04-05 11:13:27"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Kadellar\" title=\"User:Kadellar\">Carlos Delgado</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}}}]},{"pageid":41692797,"title":"File:Cicindela duponti in Kadavoor.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Cicindela_duponti_in_Kadavoor.jpg/960px-Cicindela_duponti_in_Kadavoor.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cicindela_duponti_in_Kadavoor.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"<i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cosmodela_barmanica\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Cosmodela barmanica\">Cosmodela barmanica</a></i>, belong to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cicindelidae\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Cicindelidae\">Cicindelidae</a>, commonly known as Common tiger beetles, are generally brightly colored and metallic beetles, often with some sort of patterning of ivory or cream-colored markings. They are most abundant and diverse in habitats with sandy soil (though some prefer clay), and very often near bodies of water, even if seasonally transient; along river, sea and lake shores, on sand dunes, around playa lakebeds and on clay banks or woodland paths."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"12 July 2015"},"Artist":{"value":"<div class=\"fn value\">\n<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Jkadavoor\" title=\"User:Jkadavoor\">Jeevan Jose, Kerala, India</a></div>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}}]},{"pageid":47219891,"title":"File:Cime de Caron France top station from SE on 2015-01-05.png","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Cime_de_Caron_France_top_station_from_SE_on_2015-01-05.png/960px-Cime_de_Caron_France_top_station_from_SE_on_2015-01-05.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cime_de_Caron_France_top_station_from_SE_on_2015-01-05.png","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"The top station on Cime de Caron in France from south-east"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"Taken on 5 January 2015"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Rftblr\" title=\"User:Rftblr\">Robert F. Tobler</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}}]},{"pageid":58327289,"title":"File:Ciconia ciconia - Heidelberg.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Ciconia_ciconia_-_Heidelberg.jpg/960px-Ciconia_ciconia_-_Heidelberg.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ciconia_ciconia_-_Heidelberg.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"<i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_stork\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:White stork\">Ciconia ciconia</a></i> <small>(Linnaeus, 1758)</small>, White stork; <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heidelberg_Zoo\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Heidelberg Zoo\">Heidelberg Zoo</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heidelberg\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Heidelberg\">Heidelberg</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Germany\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Germany\">Germany</a>."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2017-04-09"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Llez\" title=\"User:Llez\">H. Zell</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}}}]},{"pageid":61394012,"title":"File:Cicadidae 2017 Koroni 08.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Cicadidae_2017_Koroni_08.jpg/960px-Cicadidae_2017_Koroni_08.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cicadidae_2017_Koroni_08.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"A cicada (cicada orni, according to <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://de.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Wikipedia%3ARedaktion_Biologie%2FBestimmung&amp;type=revision&amp;diff=167753788&amp;oldid=167752135\">WP:de/Redaktion Biologie/Bestimmung</a>) on an olive tree near Koroni, Greece"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2017-07-23 16:51:55"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Sputniktilt\" title=\"User:Sputniktilt\">Sputniktilt</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}}]},{"pageid":68567185,"title":"File:Cicada exuvia.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Cicada_exuvia.jpg/960px-Cicada_exuvia.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cicada_exuvia.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/exuviae\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:exuviae\">Exuvia</a> of a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cicada\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Cicada\"><i>cicadidae</i> (cicada)</a> from Laos. Rear view, top view, ventral view, and three-quarter view."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2018-04-25 13:55:06"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Basile_Morin\" title=\"User:Basile Morin\">Basile Morin</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}}]},{"pageid":85502477,"title":"File:Ciechanów, wieżowy zbiornik wyrównawczy (3).jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Ciechan%C3%B3w%2C_wie%C5%BCowy_zbiornik_wyr%C3%B3wnawczy_%283%29.jpg/960px-Ciechan%C3%B3w%2C_wie%C5%BCowy_zbiornik_wyr%C3%B3wnawczy_%283%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ciechan%C3%B3w,_wie%C5%BCowy_zbiornik_wyr%C3%B3wnawczy_(3).jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Water tower in <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Ciechan%C3%B3w\" title=\"Ciechanów\">Ciechanów</a>\n designed by Jerzy Michał Bogusławski in 1972."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2019-12-29 14:34"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:1bumer\" title=\"User:1bumer\">1bumer</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}}]},{"pageid":89195676,"title":"File:Cicadidae with exuvia, immediately after moulting, in Laos, front view.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Cicadidae_with_exuvia%2C_immediately_after_moulting%2C_in_Laos%2C_front_view.jpg/960px-Cicadidae_with_exuvia%2C_immediately_after_moulting%2C_in_Laos%2C_front_view.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cicadidae_with_exuvia,_immediately_after_moulting,_in_Laos,_front_view.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cicada\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Cicada\"><i>Cicadidae</i></a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dundubia\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Dundubia\"><i>Dundubia</i></a> (cicada) standing next to its <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/exuviae\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:exuviae\">exuvia</a>, immediately after <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/moulting\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:moulting\">moulting</a>, front view. Seen on the island of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Don_Det\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Don Det\">Don Det</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Si_Phan_Don\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Si Phan Don\">Si Phan Don</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laos\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Laos\">Laos</a>. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Focus_stacking\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Focus stacking\">Focus stacking</a> from 18 pictures. The body (without wings) measures approximately 35 mm (1.4 in). The species could be <i>Dundubia jacoona</i>  (Distant, 1888) or <i>Dundubia oopaga</i> (Distant, 1881), uncertain identification since the colors are not yet definitive."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2020-03-27 06:58:28"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Basile_Morin\" title=\"User:Basile Morin\">Basile Morin</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}}]},{"pageid":89195678,"title":"File:Cicadidae with exuvia, immediately after moulting, in Laos, side view.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Cicadidae_with_exuvia%2C_immediately_after_moulting%2C_in_Laos%2C_side_view.jpg/960px-Cicadidae_with_exuvia%2C_immediately_after_moulting%2C_in_Laos%2C_side_view.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cicadidae_with_exuvia,_immediately_after_moulting,_in_Laos,_side_view.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cicada\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Cicada\"><i>Cicadidae</i></a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dundubia\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Dundubia\"><i>Dundubia</i></a> (cicada) standing next to its <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/exuviae\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:exuviae\">exuvia</a>, immediately after <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/moulting\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:moulting\">moulting</a>, side view. Seen on the island of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Don_Det\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Don Det\">Don Det</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Si_Phan_Don\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Si Phan Don\">Si Phan Don</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laos\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Laos\">Laos</a>. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Focus_stacking\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Focus stacking\">Focus stacking</a> from 8 pictures. The body (without wings) measures approximately 35 mm (1.4 in). The species could be <i>Dundubia jacoona</i>  (Distant, 1888) or <i>Dundubia oopaga</i> (Distant, 1881), difficult identification since the colors are not yet definitive."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2020-03-27 06:20:58"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Basile_Morin\" title=\"User:Basile Morin\">Basile Morin</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}}]},{"pageid":150950611,"title":"File:Cicada killer (73200).jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Cicada_killer_%2873200%29.jpg/960px-Cicada_killer_%2873200%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cicada_killer_(73200).jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Cicada killer on a black-eyed susan"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2024-07-27 17:28:23"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Rhododendrites\" title=\"User:Rhododendrites\">Rhododendrites</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}}]},{"pageid":170397192,"title":"File:Cicada-Sitia-Lasithi-Crete-Greece.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Cicada-Sitia-Lasithi-Crete-Greece.jpg/960px-Cicada-Sitia-Lasithi-Crete-Greece.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cicada-Sitia-Lasithi-Crete-Greece.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Cicada on a branch of a Laurus nobilis. Sitia, Crete, 